{"ref":"relic:chaos-altemanna","lead":[{"k":"p","c":["Chaos Altemanna is a relic located in ",{"t":"Tiny Bridge","r":"stage:tiny-bridge"},". Once collected, it permanently allows ",{"i":"Sprite-O'Sole_Meeo.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"character:o-sole-meeo"}," ",{"t":"O'Sole Meeo","r":"character:o-sole-meeo"}," to morph ",{"i":"Sprite-Celestial_Dusting.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"weapon:celestial-dusting"}," ",{"t":"Celestial Dusting","r":"weapon:celestial-dusting"}," into ",{"i":"Sprite-Profusione_D'Amore.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"weapon:profusione-d-amore"}," ",{"t":"Profusione D'Amore","r":"weapon:profusione-d-amore"}," upon reaching level 80."]}],"infobox":[{"title":"Relic","rows":[{"label":"Release","cells":[["19 October 2023 (Update)"]]},{"label":"ID","cells":[["RELIC_ALTEMANNA"]]},{"label":"Effects","cells":[["Morphs ",{"t":"O'Sole Meeo","r":"character:o-sole-meeo"}," at level 80 into a stronger form that evolves its ",{"t":"main weapon","r":"weapon:profusione-d-amore"},"."]]},{"label":"Location","cells":[["Located in ",{"t":"Tiny Bridge","r":"stage:tiny-bridge"},"."]]}]}],"sections":[{"id":"obtaining","title":"Obtaining","blocks":[{"k":"p","c":["Chaos Altemanna is located to the west of the starting area in ",{"t":"Tiny Bridge","r":"stage:tiny-bridge"},". Its location is tracked by a green arrow on the player's screen. Once collected, it will no longer appear on the map."]},{"k":"p","c":["Alternatively, Chaos Altemanna can be unlocked in the ",{"i":"Sprite-Forbidden_Scrolls_of_Morbane.png","w":16,"h":16,"r":"relic:forbidden-scrolls-of-morbane"}," ",{"t":"Forbidden Scrolls of Morbane","r":"relic:forbidden-scrolls-of-morbane"}," by casting the spell \"chapatribe\"."]}],"subs":[]},{"id":"update-history","title":"Update history","blocks":[{"k":"p","c":["This information has been manually compiled. Some updates may not be included yet."]},{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["update 19 October 2023 (Update):"],"sub":{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["Added to game."]}]}}]}],"subs":[]},{"id":"trivia","title":"Trivia","blocks":[{"k":"ul","items":[{"c":["Chaos Altemanna, ",{"i":"Sprite-Chaos_Malachite.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"relic:chaos-malachite"}," ",{"t":"Chaos Malachite","r":"relic:chaos-malachite"},", ",{"i":"Sprite-Chaos_Rosalia.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"relic:chaos-rosalia"}," ",{"t":"Chaos Rosalia","r":"relic:chaos-rosalia"},", and ",{"i":"Sprite-Chaos_Lazulia.png","w":24,"h":24,"r":"relic:chaos-lazulia"}," ",{"t":"Chaos Lazulia","r":"relic:chaos-lazulia"}," are likely references to the ",{"t":"Chaos Emeralds","x":"https://sonic.fandom.com/wiki/Chaos_Emerald"}," from the ",{"t":"Sonic the Hedgehog","x":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonic_the_Hedgehog"}," game series. They are gems that hold miraculous powers, one of the most well known being the ability to initiate super transformations."]},{"c":["The spell \"chapatribe\" is a reference to the ",{"t":"Chapa tribe","x":"https://sagawiki.org/wiki/Chapa_tribe"},", a tribe of rodent-like humanoids from ",{"t":"Unlimited Saga","x":"https://sagawiki.org/wiki/Unlimited_Saga"},"."]}]}],"subs":[]}]}